  "text_md": "Using the formula just proved,\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n38. Proof of IX, X, XI, and XII. - Differentiating both sides of the equation\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nand using the formulas just proved for the differentials of sin u and cos u,\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nBy differentiating both sides of the equations\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nand using the formulas for the differentials of sin u and cos u t we obtain the differentials of cot u, sec u and esc u.\n\nExample 1. y = sin 2 (x 2 + 3).\n\nSince\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nwe use the formula for u 2 and so get\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nEx. 2. ?/ = sec 2 x tan 2 x.\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n## EXERCISES\n\nIn the following exorcises show that the derivatives and differentials have the values given:\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nM",
